# Reduction of sorting to simple polygon proof

exercise_id: https://github.com/CSSPLICE/peml-feasibility-examples/blob/main/parsons/pb-sort2simplepolygon.peml

title: Reduction of SORTING to SIMPLE POLYGON
author: Cliff Shaffer
license.id: MIT
license.owner.name: Cliff Shaffer
license.owner.email: shaffer@vt.edu

tags.topics: PEML reduction

settings.grader.type: order

instructions:----------
Show the steps to prove that the SORTING problem can be reduced to the SIMPLE POLYGON problem.
----------

[systems]
language: natural

[.assets.code.blocks.content]
blockid: start
display: Start with an input instance to SORTING (an array of records).
depends:

blockid: d1
display: Start with an input instance to SIMPLE POLYGON (an array of points).
depends: -1

blockid: t1
display: Define a transformation that converts an arbitrary instance of SORTING to some instance of SIMPLE POLYGON.
depends: start

blockid: d3
display: Define a transformation that converts an arbitrary instance of SIMPLE POLYGON to some instance of SORTING.
depends: -1

blockid: pairingin
display: Feed to SIMPLE POLYGON the following array of points: For each record to SORTING with value $x_i$, replace it with a point of value $(x_i, \sqrt{M^2 - x_i^2})$ where $M$ is the maximum value in the original array to be sorted.
depends: t1

blockid: pairing
display: Compute SIMPLE POLYGON on its input. The result is <b>SLN'</b>, an array of points that form a simple polygon.
depends: pairingin

blockid: t2
display: Convert <b>SLN'</b> to array <b>SLN</b>, the solution to SORTING, by finding the index in <b>SLN'</b> with the smallest $x$ value. Starting from that index, take all of the points in order (cycling around at the end of the array).
depends: pairing

blockid: finish
display: Return SLN, the solution to SORTING.
depends: t2

blockid: d4
display: Return SLN, the solution to PAIRING.
depends: -1
[]
[]
